### WebSocket endpoints (reference)
# /ws/chat has been REMOVED. Pipeline execution is now driven entirely over
# REST + SSE — see tools/api/runs/*.run.http for the executable, end-to-end
# httpyac integration tests:
#   - POST   /api/runs                      launch a run (was: WS "run_pipeline")
#   - GET    /api/runs/{id}/events/stream    live SSE event stream (replaces /ws/chat entirely)
#   - POST   /api/runs/{id}/answers          submit clarify responses (was: WS "submit_questionnaire")
#   - POST   /api/runs/{id}/gate             resolve a Human_Gate review (was: WS "approve_review")
#   - POST   /api/runs/{id}/revisions        start a revision run (was: WS "run_revision")
#   - POST   /api/runs/{id}/cancel           cancel a running pipeline
#   - POST   /api/runs/{id}/resume           resume a run from a failed state
# See tools/api/endpoints/runs.http for these as plain REST Client requests
# (everything except /events/stream, which needs a client that can consume
# text/event-stream — REST Client can't; httpyac's `SSE` method can).
#
# The only WebSocket endpoint still live in this backend is unrelated to
# pipeline execution:
#
# ws://localhost:8000/ws/handoff/{{handoffToken}}
# Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: bearer.{{jwt}}, flowin.v1
